From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: bcmbca: link Cortex-A7 kernels at TEXT_OFFSET 0x18000

Broadcom CFE on BCM47622/BCM6755 (and siblings) decompresses an LZMA
compressed raw kernel image to the load address from its header and
passes its device tree at physical 0x8000, leaving about 32 KiB for it.
With the default TEXT_OFFSET of 0x8000 the kernel and its initial page
tables (0x4000-0x8000) would overwrite that device tree.

Use TEXT_OFFSET 0x18000 like the vendor kernel does, so the initial page
tables end up at 0x14000 and the device tree passed by CFE survives.

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/Makefile
@@ -160,6 +160,8 @@
 # during boot, and this offset is critical to the functioning of
 # kexec-tools.
 textofs-y	:= 0x00008000
+# Broadcom CFE passes the DTB at 0x8000, keep the kernel clear of it
+textofs-$(CONFIG_ARCH_BCMBCA_CORTEXA7) := 0x00018000
 # RTD1195 has Boot ROM at start of address space
 textofs-$(CONFIG_ARCH_REALTEK)  := 0x00108000
 # SA1111 DMA bug: we don't want the kernel to live in precious DMA-able memory
